## 7. WebSocket documentation boundary

OpenAPI describes HTTP APIs, not STOMP/WebSocket messaging.

Do NOT try to represent STOMP subscriptions as fake REST endpoints.

Instead, add a concise note to README.md or DESIGN.md explaining that:

    /ws

is the authenticated STOMP/WebSocket endpoint and is outside the OpenAPI REST specification.

Document the existing topics at a high level if useful, using the ACTUAL current implementation, for example:

    /topic/workspace/{workspaceId}/areas
    /topic/workspace/{workspaceId}/presence

Do not invent topic names.

No AsyncAPI dependency or AsyncAPI document is required for this task.

## 8. Error contract

The project already has a centralized GlobalExceptionHandler and an existing error response contract.

Swagger should document the EXISTING error DTO/schema rather than inventing a second error format.

Inspect:

    GlobalExceptionHandler
    error response DTO(s)
    exception classes

Document important responses such as:

    400
    401
    403
    404
    409
    429

only where they are actually possible for the endpoint.

Do not mechanically attach every possible HTTP status to every operation.

Examples that should be represented where applicable:

    INVALID_GEOMETRY
    VERSION_CONFLICT
    AREA_NOT_DELETED
    rate-limit rejection
    workspace deletion authorization errors

Use the actual error codes currently implemented.

